From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libs: C library for homebrew with a stand-in libc.prx

PS5 homebrew built with the ps5-native-app-boilerplate (Snes9x PS5 and
others) ships a sce_module/libc.prx whose exports all return 0; the console
binds those imports to its own C library. libs/libcCompat.cpp provides that C
library (heap, strings, numbers, stdio on host FILE*, printf/scanf, 16-bit
wide characters, stdin/stdout/stderr). The runtime linker uses it only for
such a stand-in module, so a real libc.prx keeps its own functions.
GuestVFormat lets the stdio functions format with the guest printf engine.
---
